  "transcript": [
    {
      "approx_t": 0,
      "text": "Think your lips are too thin? This is the mouth you're picturing. And it was never about size."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 5,
      "text": "Lips are not a feature. They are the line the lower face is measured from."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 11,
      "text": "Your eye never measures a feature alone. It measures the gaps around it. Move the lip line and every gap moves."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 23,
      "text": "One. The gap between nose and lip. Full lips make it short. Thin lips, long. The nose isn't what changed."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 33,
      "text": "Two. The chin reads stronger. The chin isn't what changed either."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 37,
      "text": "Here is that range, on one face. Watch the gap, not the lips."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 44,
      "text": "Now turn it. A front photograph hides it."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 47,
      "text": "None of this means fuller is better. It means lips are load-bearing. On many faces, less is the change."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 54,
      "text": "Do it now. Roll your lips inward and hold. Watch your chin arrive."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 59,
      "text": "You will not get that mouth. See it on your own face first. A preview, not a promise. Search Refina AI."
    }
  ],
